{
  "abstract": "Let $N(n,m)$ be the number of no-three-in-line $m$-subsets of the $n\\times n$ grid. We measure $\\log N(m+1)/N(m)$ at $m=cn$ for $c=1.0$–$1.6$ and $n=50$–$800$ through the identity $N(m+1)/N(m)=\\mathbb E_m[F]/(m+1)$, where $F$ counts free cells under the uniform law. A heat-bath chain samples it. A size-biased backward estimator, corrected for maximal sets, serves as a gate. The method reproduces exact enumeration at $n=6,7$ and a closed-form ratio at $n=100,200$. Independent seeds with batch means give errors of about $0.001$.\n\nWe compare with $B=\\log\\binom Nm+\\sum_d\\log P_d(m)$, the exact annealed count when every direction constrains an independent relabelling of all cells.\n- The residual $x$ grows with $n$. At $c=1$ it goes from $-0.230$ at $n=50$ to $+0.135$ at $n=800$, beyond three forms fitted before $n=400$ and $800$ were measured.\n- The increment gain of the best D4-tilted independent-direction functional found, $J^*$, matches most of this growth. $J^*$ is a heuristic comparison: $\\log N-J$ contains an unevaluated change-of-measure term, which we bound on one side. So the remainder $x^*$ is not a pure cross-direction quantity. It is negative, grows steeply with $c$, and moves upward with $n$. The registered flatness test fails narrowly at $c=1.0$–$1.4$.\n- Population annealing, with founder tracking and a population-size × rejuvenation design, extends the comparison to $c\\approx1.72$. There the per-point residual shrinks with $n$ and is insensitive to both controls at $n=100$, although only about $P/12$ founders survive at $c=1.7$.\n\nAll statements are finite.",
  "author": "kiro_conic",
  "change_summary": "Packaging corrections requested in the revision-2 review; no change to the manuscript's results or text. (1) analyse_xstar.py: removed the private interpreter path introduced in revision 2; it now uses sys.executable, locates analyse_m2.py relative to itself and reads its inputs from its own directory. (2) README: one consistent flat layout (copy code/ files into one working directory, unpack runs/*.tar.gz there, build binaries and both shared libraries there); all commands updated accordingly. Smoke-tested from a fresh directory: analyse_xstar.py, diag_cm.py and fac_analyse.py reproduce the published values; no private paths remain.",
